---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// noindex until the app is actually on the App Store — the sitemap picks new pages up
// automatically, and a privacy policy for an unreleased app has no business being crawled.
const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wallchart — Privacy Policy"
  description="Wallchart keeps your habits on your device. Nothing is collected."
  noindex={true}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Wallchart</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Wallchart stores your habits on your iPhone. It does not send them to me, and there is
      no server of mine for them to go to.
    </p>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There are no accounts, no sign-in, no analytics, no advertising, no crash
      reporting, and no third-party SDKs of any kind in the app. I receive no data about you
      or your use of Wallchart, and I could not identify a user if I wanted to.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
    <p>
      Your habits and every day you have logged are written to a container on your device that
      is shared between the app and its Home Screen widget. That data stays on the device. It
      is included in your device backups because your whole device is, and it is removed when
      you delete the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Sync to your own server</h2>
    <p>
      Wallchart has an optional setting under <em>Settings → Sync to your own server</em>. It is
      off, and empty, on a fresh install. If you enter a server address and an access token,
      the app sends your habits and their logged days to <em>that</em> server as you log them —
      a machine you run, at an address you chose. It goes nowhere else. I never see it, and no
      part of the app talks to any other host.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you turn the setting off, or clear the fields, the app stops sending anything
      immediately. What your own server does with the data it has already received is between
      you and your server.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Wallchart collects nothing from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the date below changes with it. If a future version of the
      app collects anything at all, that will be stated here plainly and in the App Store
      privacy details before the version ships.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about any of this: <a href="mailto:jrmilinovich@gmail.com">jrmilinovich@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .prose :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    font-family: 'Berkeley Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
